---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import Comparison from "../components/Comparison.astro";
---
<BaseLayout title="Redact the information. Rethink the ink.">
<div class="shell">
  <section class="opening" aria-labelledby="page-title">
    <div class="document-line"><span>A proposal for printed public records</span><span class="status-label">For consideration</span></div>
    <h1 id="page-title">Redact the information.<br /><span class="outlined-title">Rethink the ink.</span></h1>
    <div class="opening-bottom"><p class="opening-intro">A black box protects nothing on its own.<br />Once the information is securely removed,<br class="desktop-break" /> could the mark we leave behind use less?</p><div class="margin-note"><span class="note-index">The intention</span><p>Keep the protection.<br />Question the material cost.</p><a class="text-link" href="#comparison">Examine the comparison <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div></div>
  </section>
  <Comparison />
  <section class="argument" aria-labelledby="environment-title">
    <div class="argument-heading"><p class="reference">The environmental case</p><h2 id="environment-title">Less on the page.<br />Less to print.</h2><span class="sample-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span></div>
    <div class="argument-body"><p class="large-copy">For a record that gets printed, a redaction is also a mark made with ink or toner.</p><p>Rethink Redaction asks a narrow question: can outlined or lighter redaction marks reduce the material used in printing while preserving privacy, legibility, and the required record?</p><p>That is a case for testing. Smaller filled areas in a drawing are not proof of toner, cost, or emissions savings. Printer behavior, paper, settings, and the number of copies all matter.</p><a class="text-link" href="/about/">Read the proposal <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div>
  </section>
  <section class="conditions" aria-labelledby="conditions-title">
    <h2 id="conditions-title">Three conditions.<br />No shortcuts.</h2>
    <ol class="condition-list">
      <li><span class="condition-no" aria-hidden="true">01</span><div><h3>Remove the information.</h3><p>Secure removal and checks for recoverable content come before any choice of fill, outline, or color.</p></div></li>
      <li><span class="condition-no" aria-hidden="true">02</span><div><h3>Respect the record.</h3><p>Retain required withholding notices, locations, and context. Follow the rules that apply to that specific release.</p></div></li>
      <li><span class="condition-no" aria-hidden="true">03</span><div><h3>Measure the difference.</h3><p>Test printed output, accessibility, and material use before claiming an improvement.</p></div></li>
    </ol>
  </section>
  <section class="closing-note"><p>This is a formatting proposal.<br /><strong>Its value should stand up to examination.</strong></p><a class="text-link" href="/sources/">Sources &amp; limitations <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section>
</div>
</BaseLayout>
